{"type":"standard","title":"Kim Schrier","displaytitle":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Kim Schrier</span></span>","namespace":{"id":0,"text":""},"wikibase_item":"Q58333616","titles":{"canonical":"Kim_Schrier","normalized":"Kim Schrier","display":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Kim Schrier</span></span>"},"pageid":58841021,"thumbnail":{"source":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Kim_Schrier_Official_Portrait_116th_Congress.jpg/330px-Kim_Schrier_Official_Portrait_116th_Congress.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","width":330,"height":495},"originalimage":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/18/Kim_Schrier_Official_Portrait_116th_Congress.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","width":2800,"height":4200},"lang":"en","dir":"ltr","revision":"1376613254","tid":"157c31db-b89e-11f1-8046-73938ef961ae","timestamp":"2026-09-25T05:00:53Z","description":"American physician and politician (born 1968)","description_source":"local","content_urls":{"desktop":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kim_Schrier","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kim_Schrier?action=history","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kim_Schrier?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Kim_Schrier"},"mobile":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kim_Schrier","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:History/Kim_Schrier","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kim_Schrier?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Kim_Schrier"}},"extract":"Kimberly Merle Schrier is an American politician who has served as the U.S. representative for Washington's 8th congressional district since 2019. She is a member of the Democratic Party. Her district includes the suburbs east of Seattle, and extends across the Cascade Range to rural areas in central Washington, as well as the cities of Wenatchee and Ellensburg.","extract_html":"<p><b>Kimberly Merle Schrier</b> is an American politician who has served as the U.S. representative for Washington's 8th congressional district since 2019. She is a member of the Democratic Party. Her district includes the suburbs east of Seattle, and extends across the Cascade Range to rural areas in central Washington, as well as the cities of Wenatchee and Ellensburg.</p>"}